00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:57.190
So as Nick mentioned, at
Google, one of the first things

00:01:57.190 --> 00:01:59.950
that we do is we
trust nothing, which

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:03.010
means that you have to secure
everything in the stack.

00:02:03.010 --> 00:02:05.740
And as we start talking
about network security,

00:02:05.740 --> 00:02:09.880
it is very critical to secure
every path, every resource,

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.520
and every access that can happen
when you're actually running

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:15.430
your services inside Google
Cloud or even on prem,

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:18.000
accessing it from
elsewhere and so on.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.260
Now if you look
here, what you notice

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:22.660
is that there are several paths.

00:02:22.660 --> 00:02:25.570
First of all, you have
your VPCs and Google Cloud,

00:02:25.570 --> 00:02:27.760
and you would typically
use a firewall,

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:31.090
