00:40:56.100 --> 00:40:58.560
So what are Cloud
Armor's strategies

00:40:58.560 --> 00:41:00.494
for incorporating ML and AI?

00:41:00.494 --> 00:41:02.410
PRAJAKTA JOSHI: That's
a great question again.

00:41:02.410 --> 00:41:06.090
So ML or Machine
Learning, deep learning,

00:41:06.090 --> 00:41:09.060
these are basically embedded
in Google's infrastructure

00:41:09.060 --> 00:41:10.710
at all layers.

00:41:10.710 --> 00:41:13.560
And so the things that
are under the hood already

00:41:13.560 --> 00:41:15.960
incorporate machine
learning and AI.

00:41:15.960 --> 00:41:18.240
One of the things that
we want to do is-- so

00:41:18.240 --> 00:41:21.390
what is our vision for Cloud
Armor, or any security system,

00:41:21.390 --> 00:41:22.530
for that matter?

00:41:22.530 --> 00:41:25.650
You want to make that system
more and more intelligent,

00:41:25.650 --> 00:41:29.020
to a point where there is no
human that's crafting rules.

00:41:29.020 --> 00:41:32.550
Or essentially, there
is not a third party

00:41:32.550 --> 00:41:34.780
that's sitting and monitoring
you to craft rules.

00:41:34.780 --> 00:41:37.380
At least something should be
aiding them in going and doing

00:41:37.380 --> 00:41:38.530
those things.

00:41:38.530 --> 00:41:40.560
And so our vision
for Cloud Armor

00:41:40.560 --> 00:41:43.120
or for a lot of the
security systems is,

00:41:43.120 --> 00:41:46.080
can we become intelligent
enough to predict attacks?

00:41:46.080 --> 00:41:48.660
And then, can they actually
go and mitigate those attacks?

00:41:48.660 --> 00:41:52.020
And there are several
initiatives where these things

00:41:52.020 --> 00:41:53.790
already exist under the hood.

00:41:53.790 --> 00:41:55.712
But a lot of our
focus for Cloud Armor

00:41:55.712 --> 00:41:57.420
will be actually
building it out in a way

00:41:57.420 --> 00:41:59.350
that our customers can
leverage it, as well.

00:41:59.350 --> 00:42:00.350
So it is on our roadmap.

00:42:00.350 --> 00:42:01.100
